From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 02:22:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvk: indirect draw records through the pushbuffer, MME within
 its RAM

0025 again, without overflowing the MME instruction RAM, plus fewer host
waits.

CS2 on 405.12 (1080p windowed, NVK_PASS_PROFILE=2): the 2x MSAA depth
prepass takes 10.3 ms for 114 indirect calls / 365 draws, about 28 us
per indirect draw, while its work is small (715k vertex shader
invocations, 523k primitives, 96k fragment shader invocations; 32-GPR
vertex shader without spills).  The cost is per draw, in the front end:
on Turing+ every indirect draw is an MME_DMA_READ_FIFOED of its record
that the front end waits for.

NVK_INDIRECT_PUSH (Turing+, default on; =0 is upstream's per-record DMA
reads): vkCmdDraw[Indexed]Indirect sends the records to new
NVK_MME_DRAW[_INDEXED]_INDIRECT_INLINE macros as inline macro data that
the host fetches from the indirect buffer itself (a pushbuffer segment
pointing at the records, as NVK does before Turing), up to 1024 record
dwords per segment.  The first segment after a barrier, event wait,
secondary or the start of the command buffer is a no-prefetch GPFIFO
entry (SYNC_WAIT), so it is fetched only after the work that may have
written the records; later segments until the next barrier may be
prefetched, since Vulkan requires the records to be written before a
barrier the draw follows and the host fetches GPFIFO entries in order.
Padding of larger strides is dropped and gl_DrawID continues.

MME instruction RAM: every macro is uploaded at queue creation.  405.8's
macros took 2976 dwords and ran; 405.9's 3303 (0025's two macros on top)
overflowed it on GB20x, and every macro call faulted (Xid 13, ESR
0x404490 = 0x80000080).  Macros a knob leaves unused are now the
builder's empty macro (two instructions): with NVK_INDIRECT_PUSH on, the
per-record DMA macros and NVK_MDI_BATCH's batch macros; with it off, the
inline macros (and the batch macros unless NVK_MDI_BATCH is set).
Measured for BLACKWELL_A with the NVK builders on the host:

  NVK_INDIRECT_PUSH=1 (default)        2649 dwords
  NVK_INDIRECT_PUSH=0                  2649 dwords
  NVK_INDIRECT_PUSH=0 NVK_MDI_BATCH=64 2988 dwords

The RAM is taken as 0xc00 (3072) dwords, like the MME data RAM and
consistent with 2976 running and 3303 faulting.  Queue creation fails
(VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED) rather than uploading more, and the
total is logged (mesa_logi, and in the NVK_SHADER_STATS file).

Checked in the MME simulator with the real NVK macros for BLACKWELL_A:
the inline macros' method streams equal the per-record DMA macros' for
strides of 4/5, 5/6, 8, 16 and 300 dwords and 1-250 draws, with every
parameter consumed.  Not yet run on hardware.
